IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Military Rehabilitation and Compensation (Consequential and Transitional Provisions) Act 2004 (Commonwealth of Australia) --
-- which Act governs a current or former ADF member's claim for an injury or disease, whenever it began: the MRCA, the DRCA or
-- the VEA (Part 2, s 7; ss 88, 89, 93, 110, 112); how an old VEA or DRCA condition counts towards MRCA impairment (s 13);
-- no double compensation (s 12(1)-(3), (9)); old DRCA incapacity payments moving to the MRCA (s 92); all treatment under the
-- MRCA (s 117); and the offsets against a Special Rate Disability Pension (s 14).
--
-- SEAT: the injured member -- the current or former member of the Australian Defence Force whose injury or disease began
-- before 1 July 2004, or straddles that date, or who has a claim or payment under the DRCA or the VEA. "My knee injury began in
-- 2002 and was made worse by service in 2010. Which Act do I claim under now? Does my old VEA pension stop me claiming? Do my
-- DRCA incapacity payments carry on? Do my old impairment points count?" Duties on the Commission are encoded as a regulative
-- rule and as what they mean for the member. Every opinion or determination the Act leaves to the Commission is asked as an
-- input, never guessed.
--
-- Edition: the compilation registered as C2026C00273 (Compilation No. 10, compilation date 1 July 2026, includes amendments up
-- to Act No. 31, 2026; Federal Register of Legislation, retrieved 13 October 2026), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A01286.txt. In this compilation "date of commencement means 1 July 2026" (s 4(1)), the
-- start of the Veterans' Entitlements, Treatment and Support (Simplification and Harmonisation) Act 2025's single-Act scheme.
--
-- NOT ENCODED. The rules that applied before 1 July 2026 (the former Part 2, ss 7-11, substituted or repealed by Act No. 17,
-- 2025, and not in this compilation): a claim finally determined before 1 July 2026 answers `not covered`. Also out: s 5 (used
-- only in s 7's timing words); s 6; s 12(4)-(8) (death, funeral, medical expenses: the dependants' seat); s 13(4); s 14A; ss
-- 22-87 (the Commission, the Board, the Authority, the Review Council: machinery); ss 90, 91, 94-109, 111, 113-116, 117A-125;
-- Schedules 1-4 (amendments).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written from the member's seat with the 2026-10-18 defaults. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Military Rehabilitation and Compensation (Consequential and Transitional Provisions) Act 2004 -- the injured member`

§§ `Questions this encoding does not cover`

-- The stable l4 has no REFUSE. A question that can reach a gap answers with an `Answer`: either `answered` with the value,
-- or `not covered` with the reason.
DECLARE `Why not covered` IS ONE OF
    -- s 4(1) "date of commencement means 1 July 2026"; the former Part 2 (ss 7-11) was substituted or repealed by Act No. 17, 2025
    `my claim was finally determined before 1 July 2026, under the rules then in force (the former Part 2 of this Act), which are not in the deposited compilation and are not encoded`

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH A TYPE
DECLARE `Answer` a IS ONE OF
    `answered`    HAS `the answer` IS AN a
    `not covered` HAS `because`    IS A `Why not covered`

-- A local shim: the stable prelude has no YMD.
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
      m IS A NUMBER
      d IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
YearMonthDay y m d MEANS Date d m y -- renamed from YMD so it cannot collide with the YMD in newer daydate libraries; see docs/ENCODING-GUIDE.md section 5

-- s 4(1): "date of commencement means 1 July 2026."
`the date of commencement` MEANS YearMonthDay 2026 7 1

§§ `Part 2, ss 88, 89, 93, 110, 112 -- which Act governs my claim`

-- s 7(1): "On and after the date of commencement, the MRCA applies to a person's injury, disease or death: (a) whether the
-- injury is sustained, the disease is contracted, or the death occurs, before, on or after that date; and (b) whether the
-- injury, disease or death relates to defence service rendered by the person before, on or after that date." (2): the same
-- for "an aggravation of, or a material contribution to, a person's injury or disease, or a sign or symptom" of it. (3), (4):
-- the same for an injury, disease or aggravation from MRCA s 29 treatment. (5): the same for loss of or damage to a medical aid.
-- The DRCA's s 14AA ("a claim may not be made under Part V on or after the date of commencement") and the VEA's s 12AA (no
-- claim under Part II other than Division 2A, Part IV, s 111 other than bereavement payment, or ss 105-106 instruments) close
-- those Acts to new claims; they are named, not encoded.
-- Pending claims: s 88: a claim made under Part V of the old DRCA before the date of commencement and not finally determined
-- immediately before it is still determined under the DRCA ("including any reconsideration or review"), subject to s 93: a
-- pending claim for compensation "under section 19, 20, 21, 21A, 22 or 31" of the old DRCA (incapacity) "is taken, on and after
-- the date of commencement, to be a claim for compensation made under section 319 of the MRCA". s 89: the same for a pending
-- VEA claim of a kind s 12AA closes, subject to s 110 (pending prisoner of war compensation and supplement claims) and s 112
-- (pending Part VII applications), which become MRCA claims or applications. (s 107, pending DRCA funeral claims, is the
-- dependants'.)
DECLARE `The Act I claimed under` IS ONE OF
    `the MRCA`
    `the DRCA (the Safety, Rehabilitation and Compensation (Defence-related Claims) Act 1988)`
    `the VEA (the Veterans' Entitlements Act 1986)`

DECLARE `Which Act governs my claim` IS ONE OF
    `the MRCA: on and after 1 July 2026 it applies to my injury or disease, and to any aggravation of or material contribution to it, whenever it began and whenever I served (s 7); the DRCA and the VEA are closed to new claims of this kind`
    `the DRCA: my claim under it was made before 1 July 2026 and not finally determined by then, so the DRCA continues to govern it, including reconsideration and review (s 88)`
    `the MRCA: my pending DRCA claim for incapacity compensation is taken to be a claim under section 319 of the MRCA (s 93)`
    `the VEA: my claim under it was made before 1 July 2026 and not finally determined by then, so the VEA continues to govern it, including reconsideration and review (s 89)`
    `the MRCA: my pending VEA claim for a prisoner of war payment, or my pending Part VII application, is taken to be a claim or application under the MRCA (ss 110, 112)`

@export My injury or disease began before 1 July 2004 (or was made worse by later service). Which Act governs my claim: the MRCA, the DRCA or the VEA?
GIVEN `the day I made or will make the claim` IS A DATE @desc The day you made, or will make, the claim for this injury or disease
      `the Act I claimed under` IS A `The Act I claimed under` @desc If you claimed before 1 July 2026: the Act you claimed under (if you have not claimed yet, choose the MRCA)
      `it was finally determined before 1 July 2026` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you claimed before 1 July 2026: whether the claim was finally decided (including any review) before 1 July 2026
      `it is a DRCA claim for incapacity compensation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a DRCA claim: whether it is for incapacity compensation (weekly payments) under section 19, 20, 21, 21A, 22 or 31 of the DRCA
      `it is a VEA claim of a kind closed from 1 July 2026` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a VEA claim: whether it is of a kind that cannot be made under the VEA from 1 July 2026 (VEA s 12AA: for example a disability pension or war widow's pension under Part II or Part IV)
      `it is a VEA prisoner of war or Part VII claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a VEA claim: whether it is for prisoner of war recognition supplement or compensation, or an application under Part VII of the VEA (the Veterans' Children Education Scheme and related payments)
GIVETH AN `Answer` `Which Act governs my claim`
`Which Act governs my claim question` MEANS
    IF `the day I made or will make the claim` AT LEAST `the date of commencement` OR `the Act I claimed under` EQUALS `the MRCA`
    THEN IF `the day I made or will make the claim` LESS THAN `the date of commencement` AND `it was finally determined before 1 July 2026`
         THEN `not covered` `my claim was finally determined before 1 July 2026, under the rules then in force (the former Part 2 of this Act), which are not in the deposited compilation and are not encoded`
         ELSE `answered` `the MRCA: on and after 1 July 2026 it applies to my injury or disease, and to any aggravation of or material contribution to it, whenever it began and whenever I served (s 7); the DRCA and the VEA are closed to new claims of this kind`
    ELSE IF `it was finally determined before 1 July 2026`
         THEN `not covered` `my claim was finally determined before 1 July 2026, under the rules then in force (the former Part 2 of this Act), which are not in the deposited compilation and are not encoded`
         ELSE IF `the Act I claimed under` EQUALS `the DRCA (the Safety, Rehabilitation and Compensation (Defence-related Claims) Act 1988)`
              THEN IF `it is a DRCA claim for incapacity compensation`
                   THEN `answered` `the MRCA: my pending DRCA claim for incapacity compensation is taken to be a claim under section 319 of the MRCA (s 93)`
                   ELSE `answered` `the DRCA: my claim under it was made before 1 July 2026 and not finally determined by then, so the DRCA continues to govern it, including reconsideration and review (s 88)`
              ELSE IF `it is a VEA prisoner of war or Part VII claim`
                   THEN `answered` `the MRCA: my pending VEA claim for a prisoner of war payment, or my pending Part VII application, is taken to be a claim or application under the MRCA (ss 110, 112)`
                   ELSE `answered` `the VEA: my claim under it was made before 1 July 2026 and not finally determined by then, so the VEA continues to govern it, including reconsideration and review (s 89)`

§§ `s 13 -- do my old VEA or DRCA impairment points count under the MRCA`

-- s 13(1): "This section applies to a claim that is made under section 319 of the MRCA on or after the date of commencement,
-- including a claim in respect of a person who has: (a) a war-caused or defence-caused injury or disease (within the meaning
-- of the VEA) (the old injury or disease); or (b) an injury or disease (within the meaning of the DRCA)". (2): "The Commission
-- must determine the impairment points constituted by the impairment suffered by the person from the old injury or disease
-- using the guide under section 67 of the MRCA." (3): "the Commission must count the impairment points determined for the old
-- injury or disease under subsection (2) towards the person's total impairment points." (4): the guide may include a method of
-- offsetting VEA or DRCA payments (not encoded).
--
-- As a regulative rule on the Commission: it MUST determine the old condition's points with the s 67 guide, and then MUST NOT
-- determine my total impairment points without counting them.
DECLARE `Repatriation party` IS ONE OF
    `the Commission`
    `the member`

DECLARE `Repatriation act` IS ONE OF
    `determine the impairment points for my old injury or disease using the section 67 guide`
    `determine my total impairment points` HAS `counting the old injury's points` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVETH A DEONTIC `Repatriation party` `Repatriation act`
DECIDE `s 13(2), (3) -- the Commission must determine my old condition's points and count them towards my total` IS
    PARTY `the Commission`
    MUST  `determine the impairment points for my old injury or disease using the section 67 guide`
    HENCE
        PARTY `the Commission`
        SHANT `determine my total impairment points` counted PROVIDED (NOT counted)
        LEST  BREACH BY `the Commission` BECAUSE "s 13(3): the Commission must count the impairment points for the old injury or disease towards the person's total impairment points"

DECLARE `Do my old impairment points count` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the Commission must determine the impairment points for my old VEA or DRCA condition using the MRCA s 67 guide, and count them towards my total impairment points (s 13(2), (3))`
    `no: s 13 applies only to an MRCA claim made on or after 1 July 2026 by a person with a VEA war-caused or defence-caused, or a DRCA, injury or disease`

@export I have an old condition accepted under the VEA or the DRCA. Will its impairment count towards my impairment points under the MRCA?
GIVEN `the day I made or will make the MRCA claim` IS A DATE @desc The day you made, or will make, your claim under section 319 of the MRCA
      `I have a VEA war-caused or defence-caused, or a DRCA, injury or disease` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have an injury or disease that is war-caused or defence-caused under the VEA, or an injury or disease under the DRCA
GIVETH A `Do my old impairment points count`
DECIDE `Do my old impairment points count question` IS
    IF `the day I made or will make the MRCA claim` AT LEAST `the date of commencement` AND `I have a VEA war-caused or defence-caused, or a DRCA, injury or disease`
    THEN `yes: the Commission must determine the impairment points for my old VEA or DRCA condition using the MRCA s 67 guide, and count them towards my total impairment points (s 13(2), (3))`
    ELSE `no: s 13 applies only to an MRCA claim made on or after 1 July 2026 by a person with a VEA war-caused or defence-caused, or a DRCA, injury or disease`

§§ `s 12(1) -- if I was already compensated for the impairment under the DRCA or the VEA`

-- s 12(1): "A person is not entitled to compensation under section 68 of the MRCA in respect of impairment suffered as a
-- result of an injury sustained, or a disease contracted, by the person if the person: (a) has received compensation in
-- respect of that impairment under: (i) section 24 or 25 of the DRCA; or (ii) the 1912 Act, the 1930 Act or the 1971 Act; or
-- (b) is entitled to, and is receiving, a pension under Part II or IV of the VEA in respect of the impairment." Note: this "does
-- not exclude ... additional compensation under section 71 of the MRCA in respect of additional impairment suffered as a result
-- of a deterioration". (10): compensation counts as received "even if the amount ... is nil or a negative amount".
DECLARE `Can I get MRCA permanent impairment compensation` IS ONE OF
    `no: I have already received DRCA (or earlier Act) compensation, or am receiving a VEA pension, for that impairment (s 12(1)); I may still get additional compensation under MRCA s 71 for further impairment from a deterioration`
    `yes, so far as this Act goes: s 12(1) does not stop it; whether I qualify is for the MRCA`

@export I was compensated under the DRCA, or get a VEA pension, for an impairment. Can I also get MRCA permanent impairment compensation for it?
GIVEN `I received DRCA or earlier-Act compensation for that impairment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have received compensation for that impairment under section 24 or 25 of the DRCA, or under the 1912, 1930 or 1971 Commonwealth employees' compensation Acts (count it even if the amount was nil or negative)
      `I am entitled to and receiving a VEA Part II or IV pension for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are entitled to, and receiving, a disability pension or other pension under Part II or Part IV of the VEA for that impairment
GIVETH A `Can I get MRCA permanent impairment compensation`
DECIDE `Can I get MRCA permanent impairment compensation question` IS
    IF `I received DRCA or earlier-Act compensation for that impairment` OR `I am entitled to and receiving a VEA Part II or IV pension for it`
    THEN `no: I have already received DRCA (or earlier Act) compensation, or am receiving a VEA pension, for that impairment (s 12(1)); I may still get additional compensation under MRCA s 71 for further impairment from a deterioration`
    ELSE `yes, so far as this Act goes: s 12(1) does not stop it; whether I qualify is for the MRCA`

§§ `s 12(2), (3) -- incapacity payments for a period already paid under the DRCA or the VEA`

-- s 12(2): no MRCA incapacity compensation (Parts 3 and 4 of Chapter 4) "for a period" if the person "(a) has received
-- compensation for that period in respect of that incapacity under: (i) section 19, 20, 21, 21A, 22 or 31 of the DRCA, as in
-- force immediately before the date of commencement; or (ii) the 1912 Act, the 1930 Act or the 1971 Act; or (b) is entitled to,
-- and is receiving, a pension under Part II or IV of the VEA for that period in respect of that incapacity." (3): the person "is
-- entitled to compensation ... for a period ... even if the person received compensation in respect of the same injury or
-- disease for one or more other periods under" those DRCA sections.
DECLARE `Can I get MRCA incapacity payments for this period` IS ONE OF
    `no: I have already received DRCA (or earlier Act) incapacity compensation, or am receiving a VEA pension, for this period and incapacity (s 12(2))`
    `yes, so far as this Act goes: DRCA payments for other periods do not stop MRCA incapacity payments for this one (s 12(3))`
    `yes, so far as this Act goes: s 12(2) does not stop it; whether I qualify is for the MRCA`

@export Can I get MRCA incapacity payments for a period, if I was paid DRCA or VEA payments for the same injury?
GIVEN `I received DRCA or earlier-Act incapacity compensation for this period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you received incapacity compensation for this same period under section 19, 20, 21, 21A, 22 or 31 of the DRCA (as in force before 1 July 2026), or under the 1912, 1930 or 1971 Acts
      `I am entitled to and receiving a VEA Part II or IV pension for this period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are entitled to, and receiving, a VEA Part II or IV pension for this period in respect of this incapacity
      `I received DRCA incapacity compensation for other periods` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you received DRCA incapacity compensation for the same injury or disease for other periods
GIVETH A `Can I get MRCA incapacity payments for this period`
DECIDE `Can I get MRCA incapacity payments for this period question` IS
    IF `I received DRCA or earlier-Act incapacity compensation for this period` OR `I am entitled to and receiving a VEA Part II or IV pension for this period`
    THEN `no: I have already received DRCA (or earlier Act) incapacity compensation, or am receiving a VEA pension, for this period and incapacity (s 12(2))`
    ELSE IF `I received DRCA incapacity compensation for other periods`
         THEN `yes, so far as this Act goes: DRCA payments for other periods do not stop MRCA incapacity payments for this one (s 12(3))`
         ELSE `yes, so far as this Act goes: s 12(2) does not stop it; whether I qualify is for the MRCA`

§§ `s 92 -- if I was being paid DRCA incapacity compensation on 30 June 2026`

-- s 92(1): applies if, "immediately before the date of commencement, compensation under section 19, 20, 21, 21A, 22 or 31 of
-- the old DRCA is being paid to the person". (2): the old DRCA continues for "a week that ends before the transfer week
-- starts". (3): "For the transfer week and each later week", MRCA s 85, 86, 87 or 118 applies (by the person's category) with
-- the paragraph requiring a claim omitted; Note 1: "the Commonwealth will be liable to pay compensation ... without the person
-- needing to make a claim". (4): if the person was receiving s 22 compensation (maintained in a hospital), s 22 of the old DRCA
-- continues for them and MRCA s 127 does not apply until it stops. (5): "transfer week means the first week that starts on or
-- after the date of commencement."
DECLARE `My category for the transfer week` IS ONE OF
    `a Permanent Forces member or continuous full-time Reservist`
    `a part-time Reservist`
    `a cadet or declared member`
    `a former member`

DECLARE `What happens to my DRCA incapacity payments` IS ONE OF
    `they move to the MRCA without a new claim: from the transfer week (the first week starting on or after 1 July 2026) I am paid under the MRCA section for my category, and the DRCA still governs weeks that ended before it (s 92(2), (3))` HAS `the MRCA section` IS A STRING
    `my hospital maintenance continues under section 22 of the old DRCA, and MRCA s 127 does not apply until that stops (s 92(4)); other incapacity payments move to the MRCA from the transfer week (s 92(3))`
    `nothing under s 92: it applies only to a person being paid DRCA incapacity compensation immediately before 1 July 2026`

@export I was getting DRCA incapacity payments on 30 June 2026. What happens to them, and do I need to make a new claim?
GIVEN `I was being paid DRCA incapacity compensation immediately before 1 July 2026` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, immediately before 1 July 2026, you were being paid compensation under section 19, 20, 21, 21A, 22 or 31 of the DRCA
      `it was hospital maintenance under section 22` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that compensation was under section 22 of the DRCA (while maintained in a hospital)
      `my category for the transfer week` IS A `My category for the transfer week` @desc Which you are for the transfer week (the first week starting on or after 1 July 2026)
GIVETH A `What happens to my DRCA incapacity payments`
DECIDE `What happens to my DRCA incapacity payments question` IS
    IF (NOT `I was being paid DRCA incapacity compensation immediately before 1 July 2026`)
    THEN `nothing under s 92: it applies only to a person being paid DRCA incapacity compensation immediately before 1 July 2026`
    ELSE IF `it was hospital maintenance under section 22`
         THEN `my hospital maintenance continues under section 22 of the old DRCA, and MRCA s 127 does not apply until that stops (s 92(4)); other incapacity payments move to the MRCA from the transfer week (s 92(3))`
         ELSE `they move to the MRCA without a new claim: from the transfer week (the first week starting on or after 1 July 2026) I am paid under the MRCA section for my category, and the DRCA still governs weeks that ended before it (s 92(2), (3))` (`the MRCA section for my category` `my category for the transfer week`)

-- s 92(3)(a)-(d).
GIVEN `my category for the transfer week` IS A `My category for the transfer week`
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `the MRCA section for my category` IS
    CONSIDER `my category for the transfer week`
    WHEN `a Permanent Forces member or continuous full-time Reservist` THEN "section 85 of the MRCA, without paragraph 85(1)(d)"
    WHEN `a part-time Reservist` THEN "section 86 of the MRCA, without paragraph 86(1)(e)"
    WHEN `a cadet or declared member` THEN "section 87 of the MRCA, without paragraph 87(1)(e)"
    WHEN `a former member` THEN "section 118 of the MRCA, without paragraph 118(1)(d)"

§§ `ss 12(9), 117 -- which Act gives me treatment`

-- s 12(9): "A person is not entitled to be provided with treatment under Part 3 of Chapter 6 of the MRCA for an injury or
-- disease for a period if the person is being provided with treatment under subsection 85(1) or (2) of the VEA for that injury
-- or disease for that period." s 117(1)-(2): if, on or after the date of commencement, a person "becomes entitled to be provided
-- with treatment for a service injury or disease under Part 3 of Chapter 6 of the MRCA" and is "eligible to be, or is being,
-- provided with treatment under subsection 85(1) or (2) of the VEA for a separate war-caused or defence-caused injury or
-- disease", then at that time "(a) the person becomes entitled to be provided with treatment under Part 3 of Chapter 6 of the
-- MRCA for the VEA injury or disease; and (b) the person ceases to be eligible to be provided with treatment under subsection
-- 85(1) or (2) of the VEA for that injury or disease."
DECLARE `Which Act gives me treatment` IS ONE OF
    `the MRCA, for both: once I become entitled to MRCA treatment for my service injury or disease, I am treated under the MRCA for my separate VEA condition too, and stop being eligible for VEA treatment for it (s 117)`
    `the VEA, for this condition and period: while I am being treated for it under VEA s 85(1) or (2), I am not entitled to MRCA treatment for the same condition and period (s 12(9))`
    `the MRCA, so far as this Act goes: neither s 12(9) nor s 117 moves my treatment`

@export I get VEA treatment for one condition. If I become entitled to MRCA treatment, which Act treats me?
GIVEN `I am entitled to MRCA treatment for a service injury or disease from 1 July 2026` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on or after 1 July 2026, you have become entitled to treatment under Part 3 of Chapter 6 of the MRCA for a service injury or disease
      `I am eligible for or getting VEA s 85 treatment for a separate condition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are eligible for, or getting, treatment under VEA s 85(1) or (2) for a separate war-caused or defence-caused injury or disease
      `I am getting VEA s 85 treatment for this same condition and period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are getting VEA s 85(1) or (2) treatment for the same condition, for the same period, that you want MRCA treatment for
GIVETH A `Which Act gives me treatment`
DECIDE `Which Act gives me treatment question` IS
    IF `I am entitled to MRCA treatment for a service injury or disease from 1 July 2026` AND `I am eligible for or getting VEA s 85 treatment for a separate condition`
    THEN `the MRCA, for both: once I become entitled to MRCA treatment for my service injury or disease, I am treated under the MRCA for my separate VEA condition too, and stop being eligible for VEA treatment for it (s 117)`
    ELSE IF `I am getting VEA s 85 treatment for this same condition and period`
         THEN `the VEA, for this condition and period: while I am being treated for it under VEA s 85(1) or (2), I am not entitled to MRCA treatment for the same condition and period (s 12(9))`
         ELSE `the MRCA, so far as this Act goes: neither s 12(9) nor s 117 moves my treatment`

§§ `s 14 -- if I get a Special Rate Disability Pension and a VEA pension or DRCA lump sum`

-- s 14(1): "the maximum weekly amount of a Special Rate Disability Pension that could be payable to a person, at a time, must
-- also be reduced by one half of the fortnightly rate at which any pension because of paragraph 13(1)(b) or 70(1)(b) of the
-- VEA is payable to the person at that time." (2): "must also be reduced by the sum of any previous payments of a lump sum to
-- the person under section 24, 25 or 27 of the DRCA, converted to a weekly amount in accordance with regulations" (the
-- regulations are not deposited: the converted weekly amount is an input). The reduction is to the maximum (s 204 of the MRCA).
@export By how much, in dollars a week, is the maximum Special Rate Disability Pension I can be paid reduced because of my VEA pension or DRCA lump sums (s 14)?
GIVEN `the fortnightly rate of my VEA pension under s 13(1)(b) or 70(1)(b)` IS A NUMBER @desc The fortnightly rate, in dollars, of any VEA pension payable to you because of paragraph 13(1)(b) or 70(1)(b) of the VEA (0 if none)
      `my DRCA lump sums converted to a weekly amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The weekly amount, in dollars, that your earlier DRCA section 24, 25 or 27 lump sums convert to under the regulations (0 if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much is my maximum Special Rate Disability Pension reduced` IS
    (`the fortnightly rate of my VEA pension under s 13(1)(b) or 70(1)(b)` DIVIDED BY 2) PLUS `my DRCA lump sums converted to a weekly amount`
